  "correct": "4",
  "solution": "The logic followed here is : **(1st number × 3rd number) = (2nd number × 2)**\n\nGiven :\n\n \n• (12, 42, 7)\n\n​12 × 7 = 42 × 2\n\n84 = 84 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• (13, 52, 8)\n\n​13 × 8 = 52 × 2\n\n104 = 104 (LHS = RHS)\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (8, 7, 43)\n\n​8 × 43 = 7 × 2\n\n**344 ≠ 14 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (7, 12, 6)\n\n​7 × 6 = 12 × 2\n\n**42 ≠ 24 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (9, 26, 8)\n\n​9 × 8 = 26 × 2\n\n**72 ≠ 52 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (9, 18, 4)\n\n​9 × 4 = 18 × 2\n\n**36 = 36 (LHS = RHS)**\n\nHence, **\"Option - (4)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n6a:Tbe9,\n&",
